===Etymology===
{{compound|ms|negeri|gloss1=state|sembilan|gloss2=nine}}.

The name was derived from nine original regions that the state formerly controlled, including [[w:Naning|Naning]] (now part of Melaka), [[w:Segamat|Segamat]] (now part of Johor), [[w:Bera District|Ulu Pahang]] (now part of Pahang), and [[w:Kuala Langat District|Klang]] (now part of Selangor).

